WEBVTT

00:00.348 --> 00:02.600
- [Voiceover] A barista
poured a cup of coffee.

00:02.600 --> 00:04.319
The initial temperature of the coffee

00:04.319 --> 00:06.341
was 90 degrees Celsius.

00:06.341 --> 00:08.872
At time t increased (laughs).

00:08.872 --> 00:12.889
As time t increased, the
temperature C of the coffee

00:12.889 --> 00:15.489
began to decrease exponentially

00:15.489 --> 00:19.042
and approach room temperature
of 20 degrees Celsius.

00:19.042 --> 00:23.384
Which of the following graphs
could model this relationship?

00:23.384 --> 00:25.241
So we're starting at 90 degrees Celsius.

00:25.241 --> 00:28.167
It looks like all of the graphs
start at 90 degrees Celsius

00:28.167 --> 00:30.930
at t equals zero.

00:30.930 --> 00:34.506
And we're going to approach
the room temperature

00:34.506 --> 00:36.154
of 20 degrees Celsius.

00:36.154 --> 00:38.731
So this first one does
approach the room temperature

00:38.731 --> 00:41.849
of 20 degrees Celsius as t increases.

00:41.849 --> 00:45.761
Now this one, when t is 70,

00:45.761 --> 00:48.199
when t is 70.

00:48.199 --> 00:50.312
I'm assuming this is in minutes.

00:50.312 --> 00:53.725
When t is 70 it looks like
it has the temperature

00:53.725 --> 00:56.209
going to zero degrees Celsius

00:56.209 --> 00:58.708
so that cup of coffee is
going to start freezing.

00:58.708 --> 01:00.450
So I think I can rule out B.

01:00.450 --> 01:03.909
Also this looks like a linear
model not an exponential one.

01:03.909 --> 01:05.657
C, it does get us to this end state

01:05.657 --> 01:07.677
that stays at 20 degrees,

01:07.677 --> 01:09.674
but it doesn't look like
an exponential model.

01:09.674 --> 01:11.787
It looks like it's linearly decreasing

01:11.787 --> 01:14.620
and then it stops linearly
decreasing after 50 minutes

01:14.620 --> 01:16.492
and then it just stays
constant at that temperature

01:16.492 --> 01:17.792
of 20 degrees.

01:17.792 --> 01:18.999
So even though it gets
us to the right place,

01:18.999 --> 01:21.507
it does not look like
an exponential decay.

01:21.507 --> 01:23.574
So I would rule choice C out as well.

01:23.574 --> 01:25.106
So A is looking good.

01:25.106 --> 01:26.964
D, we are starting at 90,

01:26.964 --> 01:30.005
it does look like an exponential function.

01:30.005 --> 01:32.926
We have exponential decay right over here

01:32.926 --> 01:34.516
and we are approaching something

01:34.516 --> 01:35.700
but it's not the room temperature

01:35.700 --> 01:36.814
of 20 degrees Celsius.

01:36.814 --> 01:39.183
We're approaching 30 degrees Celsius here.

01:39.183 --> 01:40.715
So I'd also rule out D.

01:40.715 --> 01:42.364
So A is looking good.

01:42.364 --> 01:44.035
It's an exponential.

01:44.035 --> 01:46.195
It's decreasing exponentially.

01:46.195 --> 01:47.843
Starting at 90 degrees Celsius

01:47.843 --> 01:49.979
and it's approaching the room temperature

01:49.979 --> 01:52.533
of 20 degrees Celsius.

01:52.533 --> 01:54.609
Let's do another one of these.

01:56.193 --> 01:57.633
So it says.

01:57.633 --> 02:00.535
Let me scroll up a little bit.

02:00.535 --> 02:03.368
So it says, after the
closing of the mills,

02:03.368 --> 02:07.013
the population of the town
starts decreasing exponentially.

02:07.013 --> 02:10.032
The graph below represents
the population, P,

02:10.032 --> 02:13.143
in thousands, of the town t years

02:13.143 --> 02:15.558
after the closing of the mill.

02:15.558 --> 02:16.324
Alright.

02:16.324 --> 02:19.691
So it looks like the
population starts at 40,000.

02:19.691 --> 02:21.130
It's decreasing exponentially.

02:21.130 --> 02:22.547
It looks like, over time, the population

02:22.547 --> 02:25.542
is approaching 20,000 people.

02:25.542 --> 02:27.391
So, what are the question here?

02:27.391 --> 02:29.573
Based on the graph, with the mill closed,

02:29.573 --> 02:31.260
what does the population
of the town approach

02:31.260 --> 02:32.722
as time increases?

02:32.722 --> 02:33.541
We just said it.

02:33.541 --> 02:36.466
As time increases, it looks
like it's coming close to,

02:36.466 --> 02:38.904
it's approaching, 20,000.

02:38.904 --> 02:41.366
It's approaching 20,000.

02:41.366 --> 02:45.313
It's already gotten
below 22,000 as far as,

02:45.313 --> 02:47.719
you know, it looks like
after 20 or 22 years.

02:47.719 --> 02:49.321
We've already gotten below 22,000,

02:49.321 --> 02:51.202
so we're definitely below 30 or 40,000.

02:51.202 --> 02:53.593
But we haven't gotten below 20,000

02:53.593 --> 02:55.613
but we are approaching it.

02:55.613 --> 02:57.680
We can even check our answer if we like.
